@brickkit/workflow-inspector

This package is derived from @workflow/web 5.0.5, the Workflow SDK's
observability UI (https://github.com/vercel/workflow, packages/web), copyright
Vercel, Inc. and its contributors, licensed under Apache-2.0. The UI components
it draws (traces, streams, events) come unchanged from @workflow/web-shared.

Changes: removed the header (logo, connection status, health check, theme
picker, docs link) and the pages and server settings that only matter when the
UI runs on its own; removed the Graph and Workflows views, which the app never
showed, with the workflow manifest they read; removed the health check call;
the page follows the light or dark theme of the document that frames it, and
takes its colors, type and radii from the Brick dev dashboard, whose fonts it
loads; the host process passes its own world to createFetchHandler() instead of
the UI building a world from WORKFLOW_* environment variables, so nothing from
the environment is read or sent to the browser; the standalone server, the
Vercel and self-host entry points, the registry file and the upstream tests
were dropped; the stylesheet imports @workflow/web-shared from npm; the client
is built for current browsers (es2022), and for the path the dashboard serves it
at (/workflows/), so that its file URLs need no rewriting at run time.
